  "query_preview": "..The surface high pressure system near the Four Corners \nwill support dry conditions, near to slightly above seasonable \ntemperatures, and north to northeast winds across northern AZ \nthrough Thursday. Looking towards Friday and the weekend, models \nshows a cut-off low breaking off of a deepening trough off of the\nwest coast and moving across Baja California. Model trends \ncontinue to support the recent northward track of the low across \nsouthern AZ, but still show this low weakening as it does so. The \ncurrent pattern predicted by the models would support some showers\nand the potential for gusty winds across the northern AZ late \nFriday and over the weekend, but low confidence on this pattern \nbeing very impactful. This system is still around about 5 to 7 \ndays away so for now the main action to take is to monitor future \nforecast trends to see if this system will become something \nimpactful or if trends continue to support a weak cut-off low with\nminimal impacts.\n\nBeyond next weekend, our attention will then turn toward the deep\nwest coast trough that the originally created the cut-off low.\nHowever, this is beyond the current 7 day forecast period and\nconfidence on any particular forecast for this trough is very low\nat this time.",
